xnu 0208: the boot logo is not painted over by the colour-bar self-test

0084 painted four colour bars when the console started, the white one
covering the right quarter of the panel from the console rows down, to check
the panel's byte order and stride from a photo. The framebuffer driver has
since presented CoreAnimation at 1440x3200 with the right order, so the test
has no reader left: what it does now is sit on top of the Apple logo until
the first UI swap, which is the white square in the bottom-right quadrant of
the boot screen.

Remove the bars and their helper. The panel geometry and byte order are
measured and in `docs/MONDIAN_GPU.md`; if they ever need re-checking, the
self-test is one revert away.
--- a/pexpert/arm/pe_serial.c
+++ b/pexpert/arm/pe_serial.c
@@ -818,38 +818,6 @@
 	__builtin_arm_dsb(0xf);
 }
 
-/*
- * Colour and geometry self-test, painted once when the console starts.
- *
- * A photo of the phone is the only way to know what the panel really shows,
- * and the two rows the console keeps free at the bottom are the only place
- * the text never overwrites. Four bars, left to right: red, green, blue,
- * white. They are written with a zero top byte, so if they appear at all
- * the panel ignores alpha; if the order is not red-green-blue-white, the
- * byte order in the ADT is wrong; if a bar is missing or starts short, the
- * width or the stride is wrong. All of that has to be known before the
- * userland framebuffer driver starts writing pixels.
- */
-static void
-fbcon_paint_colour_bars(void)
-{
-	static const uint32_t bars[4] = {
-		0x00ff0000u,            /* red */
-		0x0000ff00u,            /* green */
-		0x000000ffu,            /* blue */
-		0x00ffffffu             /* white */
-	};
-	uint32_t y0 = fbcon_rows * 16 * FBCON_SCALE;
-
-	for (uint32_t y = y0; y < fbcon_height; y++) {
-		volatile uint32_t *line = fbcon_base + y * (fbcon_stride / 4);
-		for (uint32_t x = 0; x < fbcon_width; x++) {
-			line[x] = bars[(uint64_t)x * 4 / fbcon_width];
-		}
-	}
-	__builtin_arm_dsb(0xf);
-}
-
 static void
 fbcon_init(void)
 {
@@ -863,7 +831,6 @@
 	for (uint32_t r = 0; r < fbcon_rows; r++) {
 		fbcon_clear_row(r);
 	}
-	fbcon_paint_colour_bars();
 }
 
 static unsigned int
